In working on the Clan trophy calculations, I hit a database result that
intrigued me, so I figured I'd expand that a bit and share some interesting
stats with y'all.

Here are some figures on how long a NetHack game lasts, calculated from all
non-quit (and non-escape) games so far:

In gametime:

shortest game:		1 turn
longest game:		167,305 turns
average game:		3,921 turns

In realtime:

shortest game:		6 seconds
longest game:		146.4 hours
average game:		1.6 hours

The total realtime used so far by all players in the tournament is 9,659 hours
(that's more than a year, more precisely it's 402.5 days).  Yow!  ;-)

